## 12. Conclusion

This paper has established the foundation of the Hodge Complex Standard Model. The substrate is the periodic 8x8 torus Lambda = Z8 x Z8, selected by the unified substrate selection theorem (Section 2.6). The substrate carries the Hodge complex Omega^0 + Omega^1 + Omega^2 with D^2 = Delta exactly on each form degree. The 14 modes at the self-paired eigenvalue lambda = 4 are identified with one Standard Model generation. The processor T and its five-layer loop are the machine's operation. The output structures (charge, mass, flavor, gravity, cosmology) are the residue after mirror cancellation.

The framework's most consequential structural results are five. First, the Kernel-Diagonal Theorem unifies the framework's three leading coefficients under a single projector: the EFT coefficient c = 5/9, the mass-map coefficient (d-1)/2 = 3/2, and the kernel dimension 10 = (d-1)^2 + 1 are three traces of the diagonal of the projector onto ker(H_wind). Second, the Lambda-promotion mechanism is closed: the residual vacuum energy is promoted by pure projection onto the timelike direction of ker D, and the hidden u(1) VEVs vanish. Third, the framework's coverage of the Standard Model gauge content (absence of a light dark photon, spin-chirality Z2 grading, strong-CP solution, Proca sector, topological protection of phi_gen) is complete. Fourth, the charge sector is a rigidity-class result: five structural constraints reduce the charge assignment from 5^14 configurations to exactly two, both with total charge -1e, and the residual binary choice is resolved by the Midpoint Sorting Theorem. Fifth, the identification thesis is closed: the 14 modes are uniquely sorted into the 14 Standard Model particles by native HCSM data, with zero empirical anchors remaining in the particle sector.

The present revision closes the physical identification of the gauge and hypercharge sectors. The A1 isotypic block is uniquely identified with physical color by a dimension-and-invariance theorem (HCSM-06, Theorem 5.4). The B1 block is identified with physical weak isospin up to the outer-automorphism labeling convention (HCSM-06, Theorem 5.10). The Standard Model content structure and hypercharge values are derived from HCSM-native data and anomaly cancellation (HCSM-07, Theorems 8.1 and 8.3). The framework now has zero empirical anchors in the particle, gauge, and hypercharge sectors.

The framework has a single dimensionful anchor (the Planck mass M_P) and derives every other quantity from the substrate at d = 4 and L = 8.

The framework's claim is that the Standard Model is what the substrate looks like when you observe it.

Physics is what the machine cannot cancel. The Hodge complex is the machine. The -1e is what the machine must not cancel.

